**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title (short) | Text (human‑readable) | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|---------------------|------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| **G1** | Fulfill Resource Delivery Request | Ensure all requested resources are collected from storages and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` (sequential) | **Achieve** | – | The mission is only complete when *both* collection and delivery phases finish, therefore the root goal must wait for its two children. |
| **G2** | Collect Resources | Robot(s) navigate to storage places, request resources, wait for retrieval. | `#` (parallel) | **Perform** | AND (to G1) | Multiple storages can be visited concurrently by different robots; the parent goal requires *all* collection sub‑goals to succeed. |
| **G3** | Deliver Resources | Robot(s) transport collected resources to the specified location. | `#` (parallel) | **Perform** | AND (to G1) | Delivery of each resource can be carried out in parallel by different robots; all must finish for G1. |
| **G4** | Manage Battery Constraints | Monitor battery levels and re‑assign tasks accordingly. | `#` (parallel) | **Perform** | AND (to G1) | Battery monitoring is continuous for both phases; each sub‑goal can run in parallel. |
| **G5** | Handle Failures | Trigger alerts and report to sector manager if a resource cannot be returned to a checkpoint. | `#` (parallel) | **Perform** | AND (to G1) | Failures may happen independently for different resources; all must be handled. |
| **G2.1** | Navigate to Storage Place | Robot moves from current location to the storage where the resource is located. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G2) | Navigation is a concrete action that must be performed before any request can be sent. |
| **G2.2** | Request Resource | Robot sends a message to the storage with the precise specification of the requested resources. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G2) | The description explicitly states that a message is sent; this is an action. |
| **G2.3** | Wait for Retrieval | Robot waits until the resources have been retrieved from the storage. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G2) | Waiting is a necessary step after the request. |
| **G3.1** | Transport Resource to Delivery Location | Robot carries the resource from the storage to the destination requested by the agent. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G3) | Direct transport is the core of delivery. |
| **G3.2** | Return Resource to Checkpoint | If battery < 30 % during delivery, robot returns the resource to a checkpoint and assigns remaining task to another robot. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G3) | The mission explicitly requires this action when battery is low. |
| **G4.1** | Monitor Battery Level – Collection | Robot checks its battery level while collecting resources. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G4) | Battery monitoring is required in the collection phase. |
| **G4.2** | Monitor Battery Level – Delivery | Robot checks its battery level while delivering resources. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G4) | Battery monitoring is required in the delivery phase. |
| **G5.1** | Trigger Alert | If a resource cannot be returned to a checkpoint, an alert must be triggered. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G5) | The description explicitly states that an alert is triggered. |
| **G5.2** | Report to Sector Manager | After triggering an alert, the report is sent to the sector manager. | `-` | **Perform** | AND (to G5) | The mission requires reporting after an alert. |

