### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title (short) | Text (human‑readable) | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|---------------------|------------------------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| **AT1** | Navigate to Storage Place | Move from current location to the storage where the resource is located. | AND (to G2.1) | `StoragePlace` | 1 | One robot performs navigation; parallelism is handled at the goal level. |
| **AT2** | Send Request Message | Send a message to the storage with the precise specification of the requested resources. | AND (to G2.2) | `StoragePlace` | 1 | The robot that is at the storage must send the request. |
| **AT3** | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until the resources have been retrieved from the storage. | AND (to G2.3) | `StoragePlace` | 1 | Waiting is performed by the same robot that sent the request. |
| **AT4** | Monitor Battery – Collection | Continuously monitor battery level while collecting resources. | AND (to G4.1) | `Robot` | [1,n] | Multiple robots may be collecting simultaneously; each monitors its own battery. |
| **AT5** | Go to Recharging Station | If battery < 10 % during collection, robot goes back to the recharging station. | AND (to G2.1) | `RechargingStation` | 1 | Only the robot whose battery is low performs this action. |
| **AT6** | Assign Mission to Another Robot | After recharging, the robot assigns the remaining mission to another robot. | AND (to G4.1) | `Robot` | [1,n] | The assignment can be done by any available robot; multiple robots may take over. |
| **AT7** | Transport Resource to Delivery Location | Carry the resource from the storage to the destination requested by the agent. | AND (to G3.1) | `DeliveryLocation` | 1 | One robot performs transport; parallelism is handled at goal level. |
| **AT8** | Monitor Battery – Delivery | Continuously monitor battery level while delivering resources. | AND (to G4.2) | `Robot` | [1,n] | Multiple robots may be delivering simultaneously. |
| **AT9** | Return Resource to Checkpoint | If battery < 30 % during delivery, robot returns the resource to a checkpoint. | AND (to G3.2) | `Checkpoint` | 1 | Only the robot whose battery is low performs this action. |
| **AT10** | Trigger Alert | If a resource cannot be returned to a checkpoint, trigger an alert. | AND (to G5.1) | `Robot` | 1 | The robot that fails triggers the alert. |
| **AT11** | Report to Sector Manager | Send the report to the sector manager after an alert. | AND (to G5.2) | `SectorManager` | 1 | The same robot that triggered the alert performs reporting. |

---

### Logical Relationships Between Goals and Tasks

- **G2.1 → AT1** (AND) – Navigation must be performed before any request can be sent.  
- **G2.2 → AT2** (AND) – Sending the request is the next step after navigation.  
- **G2.3 → AT3** (AND) – Waiting for retrieval follows the request.  
- **G4.1 → AT4** (AND) – Battery monitoring during collection is continuous.  
- **G4.1 → AT5** (AND) – If battery < 10 % robot goes to recharging station.  
- **G4.1 → AT6** (AND) – After recharging, mission reassignment occurs.  
- **G3.1 → AT7** (AND) – Transporting the resource is performed after collection.  
- **G4.2 → AT8** (AND) – Battery monitoring during delivery.  
- **G3.2 → AT9** (AND) – Returning to checkpoint when battery < 30 %.  
- **G5.1 → AT10** (AND) – Alert is triggered if return fails.  
- **G5.2 → AT11** (AND) – Report follows the alert.  

All relations are **AND** because each sub‑goal or task must be satisfied for the parent goal to succeed, reflecting the mission’s requirement that *all* resources be collected and delivered, battery constraints respected, and failures handled. The runtime annotations (`#` for parallel sub‑goals, `;` for sequential root goal, `-` for leaf goals/tasks) are chosen to mirror the description: collection and delivery can run in parallel across multiple robots, while the overall mission waits for both phases to finish. No fallback is needed because the description does not specify alternative strategies beyond re‑assignment when battery is low.
